\begin_layout Title
Introduction, History, and Methodology of Experimental Economics
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section*
Introduction
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset space \quad{}
\end_inset

An 
\series bold
\emph on
experiment
\series default
\emph default
 is a scientific procedure undertaken to make a discovery, test a hypothesis,
 or demonstrate a known fact.
 But why are experiments necessary? In order to have theory, you need to
 refine said theory with data.
 So, it becomes useful and relevant to run experiments in order to test
 theories.
 Important to note, an experiment does not have to test a naturally occuring
 process.
 Yet, all experiments should try to use real stimuli and actual incentives
 whenever possible.
\end_layout

